# SwiftUI Post-Edit Quality Check

After every SwiftUI View change (even single-file), run this check silently before reporting done. Fix findings immediately — do not ask.

- No magic numbers in `.alignmentGuide`, `.offset`, or `.padding` for cross-container alignment
- Related UI elements (icon + chevron, label + value) in the same container
- Short labels (< 10 chars) use `.fixedSize()`
- Tap targets have >= 8pt spacing and `.contentShape(Rectangle())`
- Labels/values in a row share the same vertical alignment
- Separator heights and padding consistent across all instances
